{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak","id":672092,"title":"Ever used one of the \"Heavy Hitters\" AKA Lucifer/Sam Height/Carpenter/God45/Zhyzhak","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-09-20T09:38:22-07:00","id":672092,"title":"Ever used one of the \"Heavy Hitters\" AKA Lucifer/Sam Height/Carpenter/God45/Zhyzhak","content":"Yeah, that..how was the experience using those?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T12:46:43-07:00","id":672303,"title":"","content":"Does the Storm Eater count? It isn't as much a character as an unrelenting engine of destruction...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T14:16:38-07:00","id":672361,"title":"","content":"Any time I used one of the heavy hitters I always made things go calm, kinda like being in the eye of a hurricane.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/359-dezeroth","name":"Dezeroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar359_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"496"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T14:53:46-07:00","id":672379,"title":"","content":"Actually played through most of the Sam Haight-related adventures (with the Sabbat pack of when we &quot;started&quot; at A Quest Beyond Death, to boot) and honestly never felt like he was a heavy-hitter so much as a enterprising - and sometimes amazingly crap throwing - adventurer/troublemaker. He got his paws in stuff bigger than he could chew in the Amazon plot and from there it is crazed gambit after crazed gambit to avoid the ganking just in the horizon, just for eveything to blow up in his face, literally, due to his ego and ignorance combo.<br /> <br /> Zhyzak? Before Apocalypse she sounded like just another generic high-rank black spiral to me. Personally always liked crazy megalomaniac Azaera from Rite of Passage, or centuries-old Harzomatuili from Chaos Factor, far more.<br /> <br /> Carpenter and God45 i have no idea of who might be, though i guess the 2nd is probably from Reckoning with this nick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-12-2016, 11:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T15:57:40-07:00","id":672431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak?p=672379#post672379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually played through most of the Sam Haight-related adventures - with the Sabbat pack of when we &quot;started&quot; at A Quest Beyond Death, to boot - and honestly never felt like he was a heavy-hitter so much as a enterprising - and sometimes amazingly crap throwing - adventurer/troublemaker. He got his paws in stuff bigger than he could chew in the Amazon plot and from there it is crazed gambit after crazed gambit to avoid the ganking just in the horizon, just for eveything to blow up in his face, literally, due to his ego and ignorance combo.<br /> <br /> Zhyzak? Before Apocalypse she sounded like just another generic high-rank black spiral to me. Personally always liked crazy megalomaniac Azaera from Rite of Passage, or centuries-old Harzomatuili from Chaos Factor, far more.<br /> <br /> Carpenter and God45 i have no idea of who might be, though i guess the 2nd is probably from Reckoning with this nick.</div> </div> </div> </div>god45 is an Utterly insane hunter (the kind of guy who sets a hospital on fire to kill one vampire. not caring about the bystanders), and Carpenter is a wraith who messed with the Hunters of Hunter-Net. killing many in the process<br /> <br /> what other heavy hitters have you guys use? Vykos? Etc...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T17:41:06-07:00","id":672593,"title":"","content":"I've recently used some major <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> NPCs in passing in my current game (Smiling Jack taking part in an arms deal with some anarchs, Tremere appearing in a vision) and the players had a solid &quot;oh crap&quot; reaction to them - but they also do that to the local DIY NPC elders. It's probably a healthy response either way.<br /> <br /> I've also played the <b>W20</b> adventure <b>The Skinner</b> (as run by Stew Wilson at our local convention) and the &quot;oh crap, Sam Haight could come back&quot; effect really worked. Sure we made some jokes, but the adventure's a great example of selling such a character as a credible threat, emphasising how dangerous and horrible he could be without showing off the OTT power set.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-20T18:53:01-07:00","id":672702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak?p=672431#post672431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">god45 is an Utterly insane hunter (the kind of guy who sets a hospital on fire to kill one vampire. not caring about the bystanders), and Carpenter is a wraith who messed with the Hunters of Hunter-Net. killing many in the process</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, Carpenter i read about somewhere, awesomely nasty guy and great example of a well done stealth antagonist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crowley</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak?p=672431#post672431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">what other heavy hitters have you guys use? Vykos? Etc...</div> </div> </div> </div>Montano, Vasantasena, Durga Syn, Rafael De Corazon, Tyler, Madame Guil, Karl Schrekt, Lucita, Anatole, Aristotle DeLaurent, Beckett, Ayisha Jocastatian, Bindusara, Lucian and some others i can't remember right now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak?p=672593#post672593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've recently used some major <b>Vampire: The Masquerade</b> NPCs in passing in my current game (Smiling Jack taking part in an arms deal with some anarchs, Tremere appearing in a vision) and the players had a solid &quot;oh crap&quot; reaction to them - but they also do that to the local DIY NPC elders. It's probably a healthy response either way.<br /> <br /> I've also played the <b>W20</b> adventure <b>The Skinner</b> (as run by Stew Wilson at our local convention) and the &quot;oh crap, Sam Haight could come back&quot; effect really worked. Sure we made some jokes, but the adventure's a great example of selling such a character as a credible threat, emphasising how dangerous and horrible he could be without showing off the OTT power set.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, the SAS, i still have to get it and maybe ST it for some good bit of nostalgia.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-21T14:29:04-07:00","id":673433,"title":"","content":"I used vykos and some of the big cammies like hardestat in Tranaylvania by Night Dark ages chronicle. Gave them each big speeches and counter arguments during the Convention of Thorns. Had Hardestat and the Anarchs in a heated face off where H threw down an open challenge to the upstarts to do anything that he couldnt defeat of do better.<br /> <br /> To which Vykos cut off his own genitalia and threw it at Hardestat, hit him in the face too. The players cheered just as assassins then shot H in the chest and ran as he got up.<br /> <br /> It went very loud to very quiet.<br /> <br /> I've used God45 in a hunter campaign. You lnow the players havent read the books when he's telling them what's going down and they think he knows what is going on and has a solid grip on what needs doing.<br /> <br /> They all started to get a little worried, which increased further and higher with them actually asking him for things to do to help and then seeing the aftermath. You could almost see in the players eyes the doubt as their minds drowned in the uncertainty of ethics and beliefs in the wake of their acts.<br /> <br /> it was finally a quiet calm end as one player read through a book and asked mid session and asked &quot;is God, God45?...this God45 right here...our God?!&quot; I said yes and the players all looked at each other..as their pcs decided to walk away... and never trust anyone else ever again...<br /> <br /> I cant think why?<br /> <br /> Albrect has been used. I made him and burnt out who only rose the occassion in the last moment possible. PCs were like 'this is the cost of being Hero?... whoa!' Which was unexpected but I liked it.<br /> <br /> Carpenter I've used as a creepy messenger. Often a public telephone will ring just as a pc will walk past it and its always the same wheezing maniacal misery stricken bipolar wraith with news on what is about to happen somewhere. Giving the pcs a conundrum or needs for action or a warning thats a set up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-28T14:22:14-07:00","id":681395,"title":"","content":"The heaviest of 'heavy hitters' that I've used in just a story (that is, not a specific ramping-up-to-Gehenna story) was... G\u00fcnter Dorn, author of <i>Das Ungeheuer Darin</i>. However, I decided that such a character, being a complete cypher without anything attributed to him beyond that book, needed more than just a name. So, I gave him more, a lot more in fact.<br /> <br /> In my game, Dorn was the <i>nom de plume</i> of Caine himself. The player characters in our Dark Ages game wound up wandering across Transylvania with this vampire, not thinking anything about him, good or bad. That aura of perfect non-threatening, absolutely what he looks like, nothing weird at all around 'Dorn' is how I imagine the Mark of Cain(e) working, anyway.<br /> <br /> ...Oh, we've had methuselae, even one or two possible Antediluvians show up, too, but those tales were supposed to be BIG affairs. The players in my troupe still don't know that they met Caine.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>B.I.G. Bird spreads the word: Anybody with a heart votes love<br /> <a href=\"https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">https://absintheandthorns.obsidianportal.com/</a></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/409-phaolan","name":"Phaolan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar409_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"478"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T10:12:40-07:00","id":682192,"title":"","content":"I never use any of the signature NPC's from Revised or even a lot of the 2e ones either, preferring instead to make my own NPC's (I don't like the metaplot and the problem is that characters like Vykos, Beckett, Lucita, Anatole, and the like are often heavily tied to the metaplot, so it's hard to use them in a chronicle that does not use said metaplot), although I have used some of the 1e heavy-hitters from Chicago by Night before. It surprisingly went well for me. The players ended up supporting Capone and Annabelle, and were surprisingly respectful to Prince Lodin (before betraying him and setting up Annabelle as the new Prince). One of the players, a Malkavian played by my youngest brother even convinced Capone to turn his back on Lodin and support Annabelle and the players' plot to depose Lodin and set Annabelle up as Prince.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1579,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","user":"Camilla","date":". 09-29-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1579-camilla","name":"Camilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1579_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T18:45:28-07:00","id":682576,"title":"","content":"When I was about 15, I ran a game where the characters had to prevent a Gehenna cult from summoning Lilith. They all became Bahari in the end.<br /> <br /> The game before that, one of the characters met Cain and reached Golconda (because why not?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-29T20:33:39-07:00","id":682622,"title":"","content":"Lucifer exists in my WoD only he's not powerful at all. Basically God decided to punish him and Gabriel in similar ways. Both of them became humans that reincarnate over the centuries with the main difference being that Gabriel has no clue about his past and good things tend to happen to him while Lucy knows full well what he's lost, no one ever believes him when he tries to reveal himself, and bad things happen to him almost on a weekly basis. Currently he's a piss poor bellhop at a posh New York hotel who has a crappy wage, little to no tips, and frequently has to clean up after/run away from some supernatural mess or other. His only real solace is that he enjoys taking part in some of the day to day aspects of humanity such as drinking, eating junk food, and rarely going to the movies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T10:01:22-07:00","id":683261,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nist498</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak?p=682622#post682622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Basically God decided to punish him and Gabriel in similar ways.</div> </div> </div> </div>God punished Gabriel? Am i missing some crucial Fallen background here? Why?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T14:21:19-07:00","id":683549,"title":"","content":"High King David played a prominent part in a Changeling chronicle I ran. He was mind controlled by the villains to kill an NPC in order to fulfill a dark prophesy and free the fomorians from their eternal prison, but it was a prominent part! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Edit to add: I also had Caine make a brief cameo at the end of my first Vampire chronicle. &quot;Who was that?&quot; &quot;You wouldn't believe me if I told you.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Charlie Cantrell</b><br /> Onyx Path Freelancer <hr />Changeling: The Dreaming 20th Anniversary Edition, Conquering Heroes, Book of Freeholds, Guide to the Night, C20 Players Guide","edited":{"userid":648,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","user":"PookaKnight","date":". 09-30-2015, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/648-pookaknight","name":"PookaKnight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar648_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"690"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T15:15:16-07:00","id":683585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/672092-ever-used-one-of-the-heavy-hitters-aka-lucifer-sam-height-carpenter-god45-zhyzhak?p=683261#post683261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> God punished Gabriel? Am i missing some crucial Fallen background here? Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not so much some crucial background as a mention that during the war Gabriel did something he shouldn't have but it was never mentioned what if anything was done to him. It's been a long time and I unfortunately lost my DtF book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3065-nist498","name":"Nist498","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3065_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T19:55:57-07:00","id":683812,"title":"","content":"I've had the ocassion to use Kemintri to mess with my players' head, Vassilissa to brown their pants, Meilge to infuriate them and the Endless Storm to give them their greatest challenge.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-09-30T20:38:09-07:00","id":683844,"title":"","content":"Don't know if that counts as &quot;contact&quot; but one of my Werewolf campaign had the PC's as the newest Pack in Albretch's court so they were familiar with Evan Heals the Past, Mari Cabrah and the Silver King himself.<br /> <br /> During the campaign they also met with Son of Moonlight (which they hated) and the Shadow Lord Margrave (which they rather liked)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2225-ganonso","name":"ganonso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-11T15:40:58-07:00","id":698004,"title":"","content":"Yes, I've had my players be the pawns of major players, who were, in turn, directly under the Influence of a MAJOR Heavy Hitt.<br /> <br /> Specifically, in my last Dark Ages game, they were working for Etrius, possessed by Tremere, while being played off of Hardestadt, possessed by Ventrue","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"",